Theorem RL-15a: ArgEscaping freezes a complete nonempty caller extent

  Preconditions:
    - Locality = ArgEscaping.
    - Each CallerUse carries a stable CallSiteId and CallerProtocol.
    - CallerProtocol is borrowOnly, mayShare, or ownershipTransfer.

  Soundness property:
    Forall nonempty caller-use sequence U:

      (P1) lifetimeFromLocality(ArgEscaping, U) = callerExtent(U).

      (P2) Every CallSiteId and CallerProtocol in U is preserved exactly.

      (P3) Empty caller-use evidence yields LifetimeBound.unknown.

    The caller extent constrains lifetime and ownership obligations without
    prescribing caller storage or metadata.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive nonempty-list discharge with one row for each protocol and a
    fail-closed empty-evidence witness.

    Part (P1/P2/P3) - caller-use grid:
      borrowOnly site -> preserved
      mayShare site -> preserved
      ownershipTransfer site -> preserved
      empty uses -> unknown
      Coverage gate: 4 caller-use cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl15a_caller_extent;
        exact CallerUse identity and completeness)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-15a by preserving the nonempty CallerUse sequence and failing closed to LifetimeBound.unknown when caller evidence is absent
